  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $\\alpha=45^{\\circ}, \\beta=60^{\\circ}, \\gamma=?$\r\n\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\because \\cos ^{2} \\alpha+\\cos ^{2} \\beta+\\cos ^{2} \\gamma=1 \\\\\r\n\r\n\\therefore \\cos ^{2} \\gamma=1-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{y}=60^{\\circ} \\text { or } 120^{\\circ}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$",
